README                                                                      (1)


								    rflib								    
          Buffer-based, zero-copy DSP library for SDR, written in C99


## Build

No CMake, no config flags to learn. One Makefile:

```sh
make          # builds librflib.so and librflib.a
```

If you need different flags, edit `Makefile`. 
`CC` and `CFLAGS` can also be overridden  on the command line
(`make CC=clang`).

## Use it from C

```c
#include "rflib/rflib.h"

rflib_complex taps[256];
size_t n = rflib_taps_lowpass(0.1f, 0.05f, 60.0f, taps, 256);

rflib_fir filter = rflib_fir_create(taps, n);
rflib_fir_execute(filter, in_buf, out_buf, len);   // zero allocations
rflib_fir_destroy(filter);
...
```

## For anyone extending this

In order to extend this library, we must follow some rules;

1. Use pure C99. no C++.
2. Every function returns rflib_status_t, size_t, or float; 
   buffers are pointer + explicit size_t len arguments, never implicit.
3. No variadic functions.
4. create() allocates; execute() never allocates; destroy() frees.
5. rflib_complex_t is the only struct passed by value across the ABI.

See CONTRIBUTING for more information.
